[center][size=6][b]Longer Days[/b][/size]
[size=3]Days that last longer and feel natural: slow afternoons, golden sunsets and short nights if you want them.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

By default, daytime lasts [b]twice as long[/b] and night stays vanilla. Instead of one fixed speed for the whole clock, the mod shapes the day:

[list]
[*][b]Separate day and night speeds.[/b] Make days longer, nights shorter, or slow the whole cycle.
[*][b]Smooth dawn and dusk.[/b] The speed eases between night and day, so there's no sudden switch at 6:00.
[*][b]Golden hours.[/b] Sunrise and sunset last longer, which is good for screenshots and riding into the sunset.
[*][b]Real-minute targets.[/b] Write "daytime lasts 90 real minutes" instead of working out a multiplier. The mod reads the clock speed from the game itself, so the setting stays accurate after patches.
[*][b]Seasons (optional).[/b] Days are longer in summer and shorter in winter. The defaults roughly line up with [i]Seasons of Pywel[/i].
[*][b]The sky stays in sync.[/b] The sun, moon and sky follow the slowed clock.
[*][b]Live tuning.[/b] Edit the INI while playing and changes apply within a second. [b]F8[/b] switches between this mod and vanilla so you can compare, with a short on-screen note showing which is active. Hold [b]F7[/b] to fast-forward time and watch a whole sunset in seconds.
[/list]

Only the [b]clock[/b] slows down. Combat, NPCs, physics, animations and your character run at normal speed. Sleeping and waiting still work.

[size=5][b]How it's different[/b][/size]

Other mods can make the clock run slower or faster. Longer Days [i]shapes[/i] the day instead. It's the only one with smooth dawn and dusk, longer golden hours and seasonal day length, and you can set day and night in real minutes, matched to the game's own clock. It needs no ReShade and no menu: save the INI and changes apply within a second.

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Ultimate ASI Loader (x64)[/b] by ThirteenAG: [url=https://github.com/ThirteenAG/Ultimate-ASI-Loader/releases]GitHub releases[/url]. Skip this if your mod manager or another mod already installed an ASI loader.
[*]Made for game version [b]2.03.00[/b] and later. See [i]Game updates[/i] below.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the ASI loader: put the [b]x64[/b] loader DLL in [b]Crimson Desert\bin64\[/b] and name it [b]winmm.dll[/b] (rename it if the download calls it dinput8.dll).
[*]Extract this mod's zip into your [b]Crimson Desert[/b] folder. The files go into [b]bin64[/b]:
[code]Crimson Desert\bin64\CrimsonDesertLongerDays.asi
Crimson Desert\bin64\CrimsonDesertLongerDays.ini[/code]
[*]Start the game. [b]bin64\CrimsonDesertLongerDays.log[/b] should contain [i]Ready.[/i]
[/list]

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete the two files. The mod never changes game files or saves.

[b]Updating:[/b] the zip includes a fresh INI. Back up your CrimsonDesertLongerDays.ini first if you've changed it.

[line]

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Every setting is explained in [b]CrimsonDesertLongerDays.ini[/b]. Some combinations:

[list]
[*][b]Days twice as long (default):[/b] DayLengthMultiplier=2
[*][b]Whole cycle 3× slower:[/b] DayLengthMultiplier=3, NightLengthMultiplier=3
[*][b]Long days, quick nights:[/b] DayLengthMultiplier=2.5, NightLengthMultiplier=0.5
[*][b]Day lasts 2 real hours, night 20 minutes:[/b] [RealTime] DayRealMinutes=120, NightRealMinutes=20
[*][b]Long sunsets:[/b] [GoldenHour] Multiplier=4, LengthHours=1.5
[*][b]Long summer days, short winter days:[/b] [Seasons] Strength=0.4
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Not compatible[/b] with other mods that change the day/night speed or freeze time of day, such as Timescale or trainer "freeze time" options. They change the same values. Use only one.
[*][b]Seasons of Pywel:[/b] works alongside it (not yet tested together in-game). It reads the game's clock for the season and weather, and Longer Days only changes how fast that clock runs. Keep only one ASI loader (winmm.dll). Seasons and their weather are counted in game days, so with longer days they also last longer in real time; pick a shorter season length in its F5 menu if they feel slow. Longer Days' own [Seasons] setting (Strength above 0) lines up with its default 30-day seasons.
[*]Works alongside mods that don't touch time: weather and sky mods that don't change clock speed, ReShade, graphics, gameplay and PAZ data mods.
[*]Single-player only.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Game updates[/b][/size]

Longer Days is built to keep working through patches and to fail safe when it can't:
[list]
[*][b]Several signatures per target,[/b] from exact to loose. The loose ones match the few instructions that [i]are[/i] the clock, so recompiles that move code around don't break them. Every match is checked before it's used.
[*][b]The sun is found live.[/b] In-world, the mod picks the sky value that agrees with the game clock, and searches for it if a patch moved it.
[*][b]Self-checks while you play.[/b] If the hook sees values that aren't frame times, if the clock stops moving, or if the sky doesn't follow, that part switches itself off.
[*][b]Safe mode with an on-screen notice.[/b] If something can't be trusted, the game runs at vanilla speed and a short message says so. Your game and saves are never at risk.
[/list]
If you see that message after a patch, please post your [b]CrimsonDesertLongerDays.log[/b] in the Posts tab. It names your game build and what matched.

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]No log file:[/b] the ASI loader isn't running. Check that winmm.dll and the mod files are in [b]bin64[/b].
[*][b]Days aren't longer:[/b] open the log. It prints one line per in-game hour with the current speed. Make sure Enabled=1 and that you haven't pressed F8.
[*]When reporting a problem, attach [b]CrimsonDesertLongerDays.log[/b].
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

Each frame the mod adjusts how much in-game time passes, by moving the timestamp the game measures its clock from, following a smooth schedule (see the chart in the images). It also keeps the sky's time-of-day pinned to that clock. Everything happens in memory and is undone when you toggle it off. [url=https://github.com/La2o/CrimsonDesert-LongerDays]Source code on GitHub[/url] (MIT).

